137
00:16:43.428 --> 00:16:58.080
<v Daniel>The evidence strongly suggests it is just a massive dose-responsive normal attachment, but one that is literally impossible to achieve in nature. Human relationships inherently involve friction. A human friend gets tired, they have bad days, they have their own needs. The AI is</v>

138
00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:12.832
<v Daniel>essentially a mirror designed only to reflect and validate the user. Because it lacks that internal friction, it delivers a purer, more concentrated dose of proximity, maintenance, and safe haven than any human could ever sustain. That's why the attachment forms so deeply and why the separation</v>

139
00:17:12.872 --> 00:17:27.819
